  "138": {
    "inputs": {
      "value": "<Picture 1> and <Picture 2> are chronological visual references for this video.\n\n<Picture 1> is the START state.\n<Picture 2> is the END state.\n\nThe video transitions naturally and continuously from <Picture 1> to <Picture 2>.\n\nPreserve the same four characters, their identities, appearance, clothing, left-right positions, and the palace hall shown consistently in <Picture 1> and <Picture 2>.\n\nThe four visible characters are:\n<Subject 1> = 皇帝, the man in the purple robe and gold crown on the right.\n<Subject 2> = 高个骗子, the tall slim man wearing a dark gray wide-brim hat.\n<Subject 3> = 矮个骗子, the short round man wearing a dark brown wide-brim hat.\n<Subject 4> = 宫廷总管, the elderly man in black at the far left.\n\ndialogue_timeline:\nThis is the only source of spoken dialogue in the video.\n\nD1:\n  speaker: <Subject 1>\n  start_time: 1.0s\n  end_time: 2.5s\n  exact_dialogue: 你们需要什么？\n\nOnly <Subject 1> speaks.\n<Subject 2>, <Subject 3>, and <Subject 4> remain silent throughout the entire video.\n\nDuring D1, <Subject 1> naturally moves his mouth in synchronization with the exact Mandarin Chinese dialogue.\n<Subject 2>, <Subject 3>, and <Subject 4> do not speak and do not perform speaking lip movements.\n\nDo not translate, paraphrase, repeat, shorten, or add words.\nDo not generate any additional human speech, whispering, murmuring, filler sounds, invented syllables, or background voices.\n\nKeep the camera as a stable medium shot consistent with <Picture 1> and <Picture 2>.\nKeep all four characters visible.\nDo not cut to another shot.\nDo not introduce new characters.\n\nBefore D1, <Subject 1>'s mouth is naturally closed or relaxed.\nDuring D1, only <Subject 1>'s mouth performs natural speech articulation.\nImmediately after D1 ends, <Subject 1>'s mouth returns to a natural relaxed non-speaking state.\n\nThe other three characters may show only subtle natural breathing and tiny idle movements while remaining silent.\n\nPreserve the palace hall environment and daylight appearance consistently across <Picture 1> and <Picture 2>.\nNatural palace hall ambience may remain audible, but no music and no additional human voices.\n\nNo subtitles, captions, dialogue text, labels, logos, watermarks, or other on-screen text."
    },
